---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout title="Shipping and delivery" description="How custom labels and stickers are shipped to the US, UK and EU: production lead time, courier and freight options, tracking, duties and packaging.">
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Shipping & delivery" }]} />
  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap narrow prose">
      <h1>Shipping and delivery</h1>
      <p>Production and delivery are two separate clocks. Production is ours; transit is the carrier's. Both are stated in the quotation.</p>

      <h2>Production</h2>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Standard</th><td>7–12 working days after artwork approval</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Samples</th><td>Quoted separately; usually 5–8 working days plus transit</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Peak periods</th><td>Longer around public holidays in China; we flag it when you order</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Transit</h2>
      <p>
        Small and medium runs ship by express courier (typically 3–7 working days to the US, UK or EU). Larger runs
        can go by air or sea freight, which is cheaper per kilogram and slower. The quotation states which option is
        being priced.
      </p>

      <h2>Duties and taxes</h2>
      <p>
        Import duties and VAT are set by the destination country and are not included unless the quotation says
        delivered duty paid. We state the shipping terms explicitly so there is no surprise at customs. If you have
        a tax number for the EU or UK, send it with the order.
      </p>

      <h2>Packaging</h2>
      <p>
        Labels ship on rolls or flat sheets, boxed and wrapped against moisture. Stickers ship flat or on rolls
        depending on the die and quantity. If you need retail-ready packaging or individual poly bags, say so before
        the quote — it changes both packing time and cost.
      </p>

      <h2>Tracking and issues</h2>
      <p>
        Every shipment gets a tracking number. If a parcel is delayed, damaged or short, tell us within seven days
        of delivery with photos of the carton and the contents; we will raise it with the carrier and replace
        defective stock.
      </p>

      <p class="small">Destinations: United States, United Kingdom, European Union. Other countries on request.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CtaBand />
</BaseLayout>
